<h2>7. Automated access and AI training</h2>

<p>Reasonable crawling for search indexing and archiving is fine.</p>

<p>Bulk scraping that degrades service for others is not. There is no rate limit to trip because there is no server-side code, but a crawler hammering a static host is still imposing a cost, and the courteous behaviour is a request every few seconds with a real user agent.</p>

<p>On training: the content here is published openly and we are aware that open publication and machine training are not separable in practice. We do not attempt to prohibit it and we would not be able to detect it. We would prefer attribution where a model surfaces content derived from these articles, and we recognise that preference is not a mechanism.</p>

<p>What we do ask is that if you build a system that answers questions using this material, you preserve the qualifications. The articles here are written so that the caveat travels with the claim, and a summary that keeps the claim and drops the caveat produces the exact misinformation these pieces exist to correct.</p>

